## Follow-up (2026-08-25) — Codex review fix (AC-4)

Codex PR review flagged a real regression risk: the AC-2 generic 800ms
per-provider timeout could mark guided-topic-narration errored on a Polly
cache-miss, dropping an explicitly-tapped lesson in favor of a lower
priority provider. Verified the claim by reading
guided-topic-narration.ts:152-197 (real await on
synthesizeGuidedTopicNarrationAudio inside produce()) and
wake-brief-wiring.ts:597-603 (isExplicitSelection only exempts the rotation
penalty, does not force-select or bypass the timeout).

Fix: pass providerTimeoutMs:10_000 to decideContinuation whenever
isExplicitSelection is true.

$ npx tsc --noEmit -p services/gateway
  -> clean, exit 0

$ npx jest test/services/wake-brief-explicit-selection-timeout.test.ts \
    test/services/wake-brief-wiring.test.ts
  -> 2 suites, 20 tests, all passing (outputs/targeted-tests-ac4.txt)

$ npx jest   # full gateway suite, re-run after this fix
  -> 706/707 suites (1 pre-existing skip), 13,358 tests, 0 failures
     (outputs/full-suite.txt)
